I left out the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `StateHandle<'seen', read>`, and the component is rejected if it imports anything else. A grant is a change to the graph definition, so it has to come from the graph, not from the node body. The enrichment call would also send untrusted feed text to an external host on every item, which is a side channel the capability model exists to prevent. If you want the grant, add `aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0` to this node's `with` clause in the graph definition, and this node can be rebuilt with the import and fetch restored.

